Z||000000||b lo 0||08-11-2001||03:48 PM||||I was recently inquired by Doni as to the vents I will be using on the GT's hood.  They are from a 1983 Honda Accord, nounted in the hood over the strut towers.  The come out with 2 Philips head screws on each one.  They are about 7-8 inches wide, and 4 inches deep, with a 1/2 inch mounting depth.  The sides are angled, so you can position them on the hood to look a little sinister.  The way I am mounting mine is I wil plan and cut the holes, and then bond on aluminum brackets under the hood to make use of the factory mounting screws, and make waxing easier (I'm painting them flat black).  This way they can be removed in a matter of seconds.  I will have pics of the vents and planned locations soon.<P>------------------<BR><FONT SIZE="1">'85 GT (in progress)<BR>       <IMG SRC="http://www.angelfire.com/ga3/audioimagery/ice.gif">       <BR>White Lightnin!  (NOT moonshine, for all you hillbillies!)</FONT><BR><A HREF="http://www.audioimagery.vstoreauto.com.com" TARGET=_blank>Audio Imagery</A>, budget-priced car audio supplies from people like Monster Cable, Sony & more!||||reg||1
